    "content": "<p>We build pages that load fast and read well. This page is plain rich text: the body a writer types in the editor, with the headings, lists and pictures it holds.</p><h2>How we work</h2><p>Every page starts as <strong>static markup</strong>. Scripts come second, and only where a page needs them. Read more in the <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/block-editor/\">block editor handbook</a>.</p><ul><li>Static first: the page works before any script runs.</li><li>Tokens only: colours, spacing and type come from the theme.</li><li>One source: the same block on every runtime.</li></ul><h3>The steps</h3><ol><li>Write the page in the editor.</li><li>Preview it in light and dark.</li><li>Publish it.</li></ol><blockquote><p>A page that keeps working without scripts is a page that keeps working.</p></blockquote><figure class=\"wp-caption alignwide\"><img src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" alt=\"A hill under a pale sun\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\"><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\">A wide picture with its caption.</figcaption></figure><h3>Build it yourself</h3><p>Run <code>bun run build</code> to write every runtime, then open the page.</p><pre><code>bun install\nbun run build</code></pre><table><caption>Runtimes and their templates</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Runtime</th><th scope=\"col\">Template</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>React</td><td>TSX</td></tr><tr><td>Twig</td><td>HTML Twig</td></tr><tr><td>Latte</td><td>Latte</td></tr></tbody></table><figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter\"><img src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" alt=\"The same hill, smaller\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">A centred picture.</figcaption></figure>",
